## Port of pumpkin-protocol/src/codec/mod.rs
## `mod` is an operator here, so a mod.rs is named after its directory (`codec` is the folder upstream, the
## protocol folder here, so the name is `codecmod`).
##
## Upstream's `pub mod`s are namespaces; here each is a module of this folder, the file names without the
## underscore. Several upstream files share one: bit_set.rs and bitset.rs are bitset.aowl, and var_int.rs,
## var_long.rs, var_uint.rs and var_ulong.rs are varint.aowl. `mod u24_type;` is private upstream and its
## `pub use u24_type::u24` is the `U24` of u24type.aowl. Nothing in the program needs this index; it exists to
## name the whole set and to compile it as one.

import bitset, datacomponent, itemstackserializer, littleendian, lpvector3d, optionalint, recipe, u24type, uuid, varint

export bitset, datacomponent, itemstackserializer, littleendian, lpvector3d, optionalint, recipe, u24type, uuid, varint
